// %%
md`## 4. Mut locals

\`mut\` is the one way to write in place. It applies to a fresh value held in one local and ends with \`freeze\`, so no other code holds the value while it is being changed.`
// %%
md`**S4.1** \`const out = mut(e)\` gives \`out\` the type \`Mut<T>\`, where \`e\` has type \`T\`. On a \`Mut\` receiver, member writes, mutating methods and \`delete\` are accepted (S3.1, S3.2, S3.4). \`freeze(out)\` has type \`T\`.`
// %%
md`**S4.2** \`mut(...)\` is accepted only as the initializer of a local \`const\`. Anywhere else, a \`let\`, an argument or an array element, it is \`[mut-bind]\`.`
// %%
md`**S4.3** The argument of \`mut\` must be fresh: a literal, a spread copy, \`new\` on an intrinsic, or an intrinsic that returns a new value (\`Array.from\`, \`slice\`, \`map\`, \`structuredClone\`). A parameter, another binding or a frozen value is \`[mut-not-fresh]\`.`
// %%
md`**S4.4** A \`Mut\` may be read, written, passed to a parameter typed \`Mut<…>\` and passed to \`freeze\`. Returning it, yielding it, binding it to a second name, placing it in an array or object literal, or passing it to a parameter not typed \`Mut<…>\` is \`[mut-escape]\`.`
// %%
md`**S4.5** A nested function that uses a \`Mut\` of an enclosing function is \`[mut-capture]\`, unless it is a local helper in the sense of S3.11: bound to a local \`const\` or declared with \`function\`, and only called.`
// %%
md`**S4.6** Using a \`Mut\` after \`freeze\` of it, including by calling a helper that uses it, is \`[mut-after-freeze]\`.`
// %%
md`**S4.7** Only the first level of a \`Mut\` is writable. A write to, or a mutating method of, a value held inside it is \`[mut-deep-write]\`.`
// %%
md`**S4.8** A view of a \`Mut\` buffer (\`subarray\`, \`buffer\`, \`values()\`, or the receiver a mutating method returns) may only be consumed at once as an argument. Binding or returning one is \`[mut-view]\`.`
// %%
md`**S4.9** \`freeze\` of a \`Mut<…>\` parameter is \`[mut-freeze-param]\`. Only the function that called \`mut\` freezes it.`
// %%
md`The cells of this section. \`s4_blur\` writes a box blur into a \`Mut\` buffer; \`s4_counts\` writes a \`Mut\` map through a local helper (S4.5); \`s4_record\` deletes from a \`Mut\` object.`
// %%
//ss: ./spec-4.ts
// %%
spec_rejects_4 = [
